    rubric: { GRAFT_STEPS: 'carrying out grafting', GRAFT_CARE: 'caring for grafted plants until the union succeeds' },
    mis: [
      ['GRAFT_MEANING', 'M_AG9_GM_SWAP', 'Calls the rootstock the scion and the scion the rootstock.', 'In a graft, which part gives the roots?', 'The scion', 'The rootstock', 'The two new words are learnt together.', 'Label a grafted seedling: root (rootstock) at the bottom, shoot (scion) on top.', 'The rootstock gives the roots. The scion is the shoot joined on top.'],
      ['GRAFT_MEANING', 'M_AG9_GM_ANY', 'Thinks any two plants can be grafted, such as a mango scion on a bean.', 'Can a mango scion be grafted onto an avocado rootstock?', 'Yes, any plants join', 'No, they must be the same or closely related kind', 'The child thinks tape holds anything together.', 'Explain the tissues must match to grow as one.', 'Graft plants of the same or closely related kind, like mango on mango.'],
      ['GRAFT_MEANING', 'M_AG9_GM_SEED', 'Thinks a grafted tree is grown from a seed of the good tree.', 'How is a grafted mango different from one grown from seed?', 'It is the same', 'It carries the good parent\'s fruit exactly and fruits sooner', 'The child thinks all trees come from seed.', 'Compare seedling mangoes (mixed fruit) with grafted ones.', 'A grafted tree gives the same fruit as its parent and fruits earlier.'],
      ['GRAFT_MEANING', 'M_AG9_GM_UNION', 'Thinks the union is the tape.', 'What is the graft union?', 'The grafting tape', 'The place where the scion and rootstock grow together', 'The child sees the tape at the join.', 'Show a healed union after the tape is off.', 'The union is where scion and rootstock grow together. The tape only holds them.'],
      ['GRAFT_STEPS', 'M_AG9_GS_CAMBIUM', 'Fits the cut pieces without matching the green layer under the bark.', 'What must touch for a graft to take?', 'Any part of the cuts', 'The green cambium layers of scion and rootstock', 'The child sees only the wood.', 'Show the thin green ring under the bark in a cut stem.', 'Line up the green cambium layers. That is where they grow together.'],
      ['GRAFT_STEPS', 'M_AG9_GS_BLUNT', 'Uses a blunt or dirty knife.', 'Why is a sharp, clean knife used for grafting?', 'Any knife works', 'Clean smooth cuts heal and join; dirty knives carry disease', 'The child thinks cutting is cutting.', 'Compare a smooth cut and a torn cut on a stem.', 'Use a sharp, clean knife: smooth cuts join and no disease gets in.'],
      ['GRAFT_STEPS', 'M_AG9_GS_LOOSE', 'Wraps the graft loosely.', 'How is the graft wrapped?', 'Loosely', 'Firmly with grafting tape so the cuts stay together and dry', 'The child fears hurting the plant.', 'Show a loose graft that slipped apart.', 'Wrap firmly so the cut surfaces stay together and do not dry.'],
      ['GRAFT_STEPS', 'M_AG9_GS_DRY', 'Leaves the cut scion in the sun before grafting.', 'What happens if a scion dries before grafting?', 'Nothing', 'It dies and the graft fails', 'The child does not know the scion is alive.', 'Leave a cut scion in the sun for an hour.', 'Keep scions fresh and graft quickly so they do not dry.'],
      ['GRAFT_CARE', 'M_AG9_GC_SUCKERS', 'Leaves shoots growing from the rootstock below the union.', 'What is done with shoots growing below the graft union?', 'Leave them to grow', 'Remove them so the scion gets the food', 'The child thinks all growth is good.', 'Show a graft where rootstock shoots took over.', 'Remove shoots below the union so the scion grows.'],
      ['GRAFT_CARE', 'M_AG9_GC_TAPE', 'Leaves the grafting tape on for ever.', 'When is the grafting tape removed?', 'Never', 'After the union has healed, about 6 to 8 weeks', 'The child thinks the tape protects the plant.', 'Show a stem strangled by tape left on.', 'Remove the tape once the union heals, or it cuts into the stem.'],
      ['GRAFT_CARE', 'M_AG9_GC_SUN', 'Puts the newly grafted plant in full sun with no water.', 'Where is a new graft kept?', 'In full sun, unwatered', 'In light shade, watered regularly', 'The child thinks a tree is tough.', 'Compare grafts in shade and sun after a week.', 'Keep new grafts in light shade and water them.'],
      ['GRAFT_CARE', 'M_AG9_GC_KNOCK', 'Lets animals and people brush against the union.', 'Why protect the graft union?', 'It is strong', 'A knock can break the union before it heals', 'The child sees the tape as protection enough.', 'Show a broken graft.', 'Protect the union from knocks and animals until it heals.'],
      ['GRAFT_PURPOSES', 'M_AG9_GP_REPAIR', 'Thinks a tree with a damaged trunk must be cut down.', 'A young mango tree has its bark eaten by goats. What can grafting do?', 'Nothing, cut it down', 'Bridge graft over the damage to repair it', 'The child does not know grafting repairs.', 'Show a bridge graft picture.', 'Grafting can repair a damaged trunk by bridging the wound.'],
      ['GRAFT_PURPOSES', 'M_AG9_GP_OLD', 'Thinks an old tree giving poor fruit must be replaced by a new seedling.', 'How can an old avocado tree with poor fruit be rejuvenated?', 'Cut it down and plant a seed', 'Topwork it: cut back and graft a good variety on the old stump', 'The child thinks old trees cannot change.', 'Show a topworked tree fruiting in two years.', 'Topworking grafts a good variety onto an old tree so it fruits well again.'],
      ['GRAFT_PURPOSES', 'M_AG9_GP_LOOKS', 'Thinks grafting is only for fruit, never for beauty.', 'Can grafting be used for beauty?', 'No, only for fruit', 'Yes, such as several flower colours on one rose or bougainvillea', 'The child has seen grafting only in orchards.', 'Show a rose with two colours.', 'Grafting can make a plant beautiful, with several colours on one plant.'],
      ['GRAFT_PURPOSES', 'M_AG9_GP_IMPROVE', 'Thinks grafting makes the fruit bigger by itself, whatever the scion.', 'Why graft a good variety onto a hardy local rootstock?', 'The rootstock decides the fruit', 'The scion gives the good fruit; the hardy rootstock gives strength and disease resistance', 'The child thinks the roots decide everything.', 'Compare fruit of the scion parent and the rootstock parent.', 'The scion gives the fruit type. The rootstock gives strong, resistant roots.'],
    ],
